## Contracts Are Tests

### A Function Under Test

```xiom
requires { n >= 0; }
ensures { result >= 0; }
fn square(n: Int) -> Int {
  n * n
}
```

### Testing via main()

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let r1 = square(0);
  assert(r1 == 0);

  let r2 = square(5);
  assert(r2 == 25);

  let r3 = square(-3);
  assert(r3 == 9);
  return 0;
}
```

When called with `-3`, the `requires` triggers because `-3 >= 0` is false. The contract caught the edge case.

### Testing Invariants

```xiom
type Counter {
  value: Int;
}

invariant { self.value >= 0; }

fn Counter.increment(&mut self) {
  self.value += 1;
}

// main test
fn main() -> Int {
  let mut c = Counter{ value: 0 };
  c.increment();
  assert(c.value == 1);
  let mut c2 = Counter{ value: -5 };  // violates invariant!
  return 0;
}
```

Creating a Counter with `-5` immediately triggers the invariant. Tests fail fast at the violation point.

